Welcome! 💻 This is the virtual machine that hosts your vulnerable service.

[1;4mDEFENDING[0m

You can find the code for the vuln services at [34m~/ad/services/[0m

Since the services are running in Docker containers, the host machine
is out of scope.

For some of the services, they'll automatically restart if their code
is edited, you might not need to rebuild the container or anything.

Some docker compose tips:
   [33mdocker compose up -d[0m to turn on the service. If you've
        made changes and rebuilt the container image, this should
        recreate a fresh new container with your changes included.
   [33mdocker compose logs -f[0m to tail the logs.
   [33mdocker compose build[0m to rebuild the container image.
   [33mdocker compose down[0m to turn off the service.
   [33mdocker compose down -v[0m to turn off the service and remove
        the database storage volume. Your database will be respawned
        from scratch on next start. CAREFUL!

A backup ZIP file is provided in case you really break your service.

[1;4mATTACKING[0m

We've provided some example scripts in the [34m~/ad/scripts[0m folder.
The INI file there has been preloaded with your team number and secret
token. Your token is there so that you can authenticate against the
scoreboard API, where you can query for live flags and submit the flags
you manage to steal.

Under NO CIRCUMSTANCES should you expose your secret token when attacking.
Do not let your secret token go anywhere near other teams' machines.
It is against the rules to abuse another team's token, but people might do
it anyways, so don't give them the chance to.

The two [34mexample_[0m python scripts in there won't be very useful on
their own, but you can use them as building blocks for creating your own
attacker script. Note that you don't have to use Python, you can use whatever
language you want. Also, you can attack from your personal machine, it doesn't
have to be from this VM.

[34m~/ad/scripts/runs_every_2_minutes.py[0m is, as the name implies, run
every 2 minutes by a cron job. By default it doesn't do anything, but feel
free to put your own attack code here. You should be scripting/automating
your attacks like this for maximal efficiency. It logs to the file at
[34m/var/log/periodic_script[0m when it runs.

Good luck!
